# P09.24 — Rust-defines-polymorphic: `#[rustc_cxx_virtual]` +
# vtable / typeinfo / typeinfo-name emission.
#
# Delivers backlog item #6 (Rust emits its own vtable for
# `#[repr(cpp)]` classes). Rust methods can now be dispatched
# virtually from C++ through a base pointer, with the Rust
# side being the sole definer of the vtable and RTTI symbols.
#
# # Scope (v1)
#
# - Single-inheritance only. No virtual bases, no multi-
#   inheritance. The vtable layout we emit matches the
#   Itanium primary sub-table: `[offset_to_top:i64,
#   &_ZTI<class>, fn_ptrs...]`, with the address point at
#   slot 2 (first function pointer).
# - Manual vptr field: users declare `__vptr: *const ()` as
#   the first field of their polymorphic `#[repr(cpp)]`
#   struct. The Rust layout path doesn't auto-inject vptr
#   fields in v1.
# - Manual vptr init: users write the ctor body by hand, with
#   an `unsafe extern "C" { #[link_name = "_ZTV<class>"]
#   static VTABLE: [*const (); N]; }` reference and a
#   `Widget { __vptr: &VTABLE[2] as *const _, ... }`
#   initializer. Compiler-automatic ctor prologue injection is
#   deferred to P09.25.
# - RTTI uses `__class_type_info` (the single-inheritance
#   C++ RTTI kind). `typeid()` at the direct type works;
#   `dynamic_cast` across inheritance has NOT been validated.
#
# # What changed
#
# ## Attribute plumbing (`#[rustc_cxx_virtual]`)
#
# 7-file pattern matching P09.22/P09.23:
# - `rustc_span/src/symbol.rs`: new `rustc_cxx_virtual` sym.
# - `rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs`: `rustc_attr!` entry.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs`:
#   `AttributeKind::RustcCxxVirtual(Span)` variant.
# - `rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs`: `Yes`.
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs`:
#   `RustcCxxVirtualParser` (`Target::Method(Inherent)`).
# - `rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs`: registered.
# - `rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs`: allow-list.
#
# ## Symbol mangling helpers
#
# `rustc_symbol_mangling/src/itanium.rs`: three new public helpers
# and two internal ones for class-metadata emission —
# `is_polymorphic_cpp_class`, `virtual_methods_on_class`,
# `mangle_cxx_vtable_symbol`, `mangle_cxx_typeinfo_symbol`,
# `mangle_cxx_typeinfo_name_symbol`. Builds on the existing
# `rustc_abi_cxx::Symbol::{VTable,TypeInfo,TypeInfoName}` variants
# which already supported mangling but weren't wired through.
#
# ## Codegen emission
#
# New file `rustc_codegen_llvm/src/cxx_vtable.rs` (~250 lines).
# Hook in `rustc_codegen_llvm/src/mono_item.rs::predefine_fn`: on
# every method of a polymorphic `#[repr(cpp)]` class, emit the
# class's metadata once per CGU. Per-CGU dedup via a new
# `cxx_emitted_vtables: RefCell<FxHashSet<DefId>>` field on
# `CodegenCx`; across-CGU dedup via `LinkOnceODRLinkage` + comdat.
#
# Three LLVM globals per polymorphic class:
#
# - `_ZTS<class>`: byte string `"<len><name>\0"` — the typeinfo
#   name. Constant, LinkOnceODR, comdat.
# - `_ZTI<class>`: struct `{ptr, ptr}` — RTTI. First slot GEPs
#   `_ZTVN10__cxxabiv117__class_type_infoE` by 2*ptr_bytes to
#   get the address point of the RTTI base's vtable (the
#   standard `__class_type_info` vptr target). Second slot
#   points at `_ZTS<class>`.
# - `_ZTV<class>`: struct `{i64, ptr, ptr...}` — vtable.
#   Slot 0 is offset-to-top (zero in single-inheritance).
#   Slot 1 is `&_ZTI<class>`. Slots 2+ are function pointers
#   to each virtual method, retrieved via `cx.get_fn_addr`.
#
# Virtual method order: `virtual_methods_on_class` sorts
# (impl DefId, method DefId) for determinism. Users must keep
# their C++ header's virtual declaration order in sync — no
# automatic C++ header parsing in v1.
#
# # Validation
#
# ## /tmp/p09-24-vtable-emit
#
# Rust-only probe declaring a `#[repr(cpp)]` type with two
# `#[rustc_cxx_virtual]` methods. `nm libp09_24_vtable_emit.a`
# shows `_ZTV6Widget`, `_ZTI6Widget`, `_ZTS6Widget` as defined
# globals (`S` for LinkOnceODR constants) and
# `_ZTVN10__cxxabiv117__class_type_infoE` as an undefined
# reference resolved by libc++abi at link time.
#
# Vtable hex dump (8-byte slots):
# - slot 0: `00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00` — offset_to_top = 0
# - slot 1: relocated to `_ZTI6Widget`
# - slot 2: relocated to `Widget::foo` — address point
# - slot 3: relocated to `Widget::bar`
#
# Typeinfo name bytes: `36 57 69 64 67 65 74 00` = `"6Widget\0"`.
#
# ## /tmp/p09-24-polymorphic (end-to-end)
#
# Rust defines Widget (with `__vptr` field), Rust ctor stores
# the vtable address point in `__vptr`, Rust exposes a
# `make_widget(v) -> *mut Widget`. C++ receives the pointer,
# calls virtual methods. Dispatch lands in Rust's
# implementations: `foo() = v + 100 = 107`, `bar() = v*2 = 14`.
# Exit 0.
#
# ## Workspace
#
# `cargo test --workspace` → 235/0, baseline preserved.

